  toc={toc}
  relatedApplications={relatedApplications}
  relatedProducts={relatedProducts}
  hideBottomCTA={true}
>

  <div class="bg-navy/5 border-l-4 border-gold/40 rounded-r-lg p-4 mb-6 not-prose">
    <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed italic">Dolphin Centrifuge supplies parts, repairs, and remanufactured Alfa Laval WHPX 510 self-cleaning disc stack centrifuges. The published marine-diesel application capacity is 10,700 L/h (47.11 US GPM) at 13 cSt and 40 C. The machine uses a 10 HP motor and operates at 5,180 RPM.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="overview">WHPX 510 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge</h2>

  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start not-prose mb-6">
    <div class="md:w-1/2">
      <p class="text-text-light mb-4">
        The Alfa Laval WHPX 510 is a self-cleaning <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold transition-colors">disc stack centrifuge</a> engineered for the continuous three-phase separation of fuels and oils. It simultaneously separates water, solids, and clean oil in a single pass, eliminating the need for multi-stage processing.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-light mb-4">
        The WHPX 510 is one of the most versatile centrifuges in the Alfa Laval product line, handling everything from clean <a href="/diesel-centrifuge/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold transition-colors">diesel fuel</a> polishing to heavy <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold transition-colors">waste oil</a> reclamation. Its 10 HP motor drives the bowl at 5,180 RPM, delivering the centrifugal force needed for efficient separation across a wide range of viscosities.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="md:w-1/2">
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/alfa-laval-centrifugal-separator/disc-centrifuge-alfa-laval-whpx-510-300.webp"
          alt="Alfa Laval WHPX 510 disc stack centrifuge"
          width="300"
          height="300"
          loading="lazy"
          class="rounded-lg w-full"
        />
        <figcaption>Alfa Laval WHPX 510 Disc Stack Centrifuge</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start not-prose mb-6">
    <div class="md:w-1/2">
      <p class="text-text-light mb-4">
        Available in explosion-proof configurations for hazardous area installations, the WHPX 510 is a workhorse centrifuge found in re-refineries, fuel terminals, marine vessels, and industrial waste oil processing facilities worldwide.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-light mb-4">
        Dolphin Centrifuge also provides complete <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold transition-colors">used oil centrifuge</a> systems and <a href="/wvo-centrifuge-separator/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold transition-colors">WVO centrifuge separators</a> built around the WHPX 510 platform for waste vegetable oil and cooking oil purification.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="md:w-1/2">
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/alfa-laval-whpx-510-centrifuge/Explosion-Proof-Disc-Stack-Centrifuge-for-Crude-Oil-600.webp"
          alt="Explosion proof WHPX 510 disc stack centrifuge for crude oil"
          width="600"
          height="400"
          loading="lazy"
          class="rounded-lg w-full"
        />
        <figcaption>Explosion Proof WHPX-510 Disc Stack Centrifuge for Crude Oil</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>Dolphin Centrifuge is the independent specialist in <a href="/alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Alfa Laval</a> centrifuges: remanufactured machines, turnkey systems, parts, and service, built on 40+ years of Alfa Laval experience and led by Sanjay Prabhu, M.S.M.E. Apart from Alfa Laval itself, Dolphin is the reliable source for quality Alfa Laval separators in this size class, including the WHPX 510 and its MOPX 209, MOPX 310, and MAPX 210 siblings. Every machine is stripped, rebuilt, balanced, and test-run in Dolphin's Warren, Michigan shop, and is supplied bare-shaft or as the complete <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-042/">DMPX-042</a> module. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with or authorized by Alfa Laval.</p>

  <div class="bg-gold/10 border-l-4 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-5 my-8 not-prose">
    <p class="text-base font-semibold text-navy mb-1">Need parts, repairs, or a remanufactured WHPX 510?</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-light mb-3">Dolphin Centrifuge supplies complete modules with pre-heaters, starters, and PLC control panels - available as the DMPX-042 turnkey system or as individual centrifuge rebuild services for waste oil, diesel, crude oil, and biodiesel applications.</p>
    <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold hover:bg-gold/80 text-navy font-bold px-6 py-2 rounded-lg transition-colors text-sm">Request a Quote &rarr;</a>
  </div>

  <h2 id="specifications">WHPX 510 Specifications</h2>

  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Model Type</strong></td><td>Alfa Laval WHPX 510 TGD 24-60</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Diesel Application Capacity</strong></td><td>10,700 L/h (47.11 US GPM) at 13 cSt and 40 &deg;C</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Rated Reference Capacity</strong></td><td>16,000 L/h (70.45 US GPM); source fluid not specified</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Sludge Space</strong></td><td>1.62 Gallons</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Motor HP</strong></td><td>10 HP</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Voltages</strong></td><td>230 / 460 V, 3 phase</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Bowl Speed</strong></td><td>5,180 RPM</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>The rated reference value is published without a process-fluid identity. It is not a water or diesel capacity. Application capacities must stay attached to the exact fluid, viscosity, and centrifugation temperature shown below.</p>

  <h2 id="capacity-data">Published WHPX 510 Capacity Data</h2>

  <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto border border-gray-100 rounded-xl mb-6">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Fluid</th><th>Published capacity</th><th>Derived US GPM</th><th>Conditions</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Marine diesel</td><td>10,700 L/h</td><td>47.11</td><td>13 cSt at 40 &deg;C; centrifugation at 40 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 30 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>9,900 L/h</td><td>43.59</td><td>Centrifugation at 70-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 40 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>9,900 L/h</td><td>43.59</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 60 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>7,500 L/h</td><td>33.02</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 100 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>7,200 L/h</td><td>31.70</td><td>Centrifugation at 90-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 180 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>5,000 L/h</td><td>22.01</td><td>Centrifugation at 90-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 380 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>4,200 L/h</td><td>18.49</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 460 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>3,500 L/h</td><td>15.41</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 600 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>2,900 L/h</td><td>12.77</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cross-head R&amp;O lube oil</td><td>4,800-5,600 L/h</td><td>21.13-24.66</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cross-head detergent lube oil</td><td>4,000-4,800 L/h</td><td>17.61-21.13</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trunk detergent lube oil</td><td>2,900-3,500 L/h</td><td>12.77-15.41</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Steam turbine lube oil</td><td>10,400 L/h</td><td>45.79</td><td>Centrifugation at 60-70 &deg;C</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>US GPM values are derived from the published L/h figures using L/h &divide; 227.124707 and rounded to two decimals. See the <a href="/technical-data/">technical data methodology</a> or use the <a href="/technical-data/alfa-laval-whpx-510.json">WHPX 510 machine-readable record</a>.</p>

  <p>
    If you have simple, routine questions: We have condensed our 40+ years of disc-stack centrifuge experience into <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge-faq/">101 Frequently Asked Questions about Disc Stack Centrifuges</a>.
  </p>

  <figure class="not-prose mb-8 md:max-w-sm">
    <img
      src="/images/difference-between-decanter-centrifuge-disc-centrifuge/disc-centrifuge-alfa-laval-whpx-510-300.webp"
